So, as I said, number on the commission invoice is not equal to the actual commission. Commission invoice amount is calculated this way:

{{Actual commission + booking fee (if any) - compensations qualified as discount - bonuses qualified as discount}}

{quote}As FO explained invoices that he receives monthly from Bolt are representing incorrect sum of commission{quote}

So, they don’t show incorrect sum, they just think it is exactly the commission amount but it’s not. 

Nevertheless, hopefully, [~accountid:63a00ef0f3e7004f77fadf98] can help us understand what data is shared with the authorities in Latvia.

Thanks for the info, [~accountid:601bc7763b1af00069e9d9bb].

Based on that, I’d advise to respond to them along the lines of:

* thank you for reaching out to us regarding the problem;
* we take such matters seriously and have looked into details;
* describe the circumstances of the area, i.e. the bike stand, common street, no parking in private property;
* as soon as we got your response, we created a no parking zone to avoid any future disturbance etc.

At this stage, I do not see a reason for us to pay what they claim.

