Paragraph 5.4 doesn’t suite in the current wording. We commit to providing backward compatible API, but “and (ii) the new/updated/improved version is

announced with a Written Statement one (1) month before it will be put into production“ is not acceptable. During the new partners onboarding we might come to a decision of introducing a new API endpoint or a new version of some existing API endpoint. Typically we release these changes as fast as possible (within from couple of days to a week). We are not ready to artificially slow down the process. Either the second part has to be completely removed or softened in a way “we notify Umob about introduced new API features“



Appendix 1

{{1.1 The agreed fee for umob is 8% on the total revenue.}}

It’s not correct we agreed on 5% in the email conversation (search for “umob catchup“)

{{2.1 Parties have agreed that a new customer will get the first rental of 10 free}}
{{minutes including unlock fee}}

We are not ready to subsidise their users acquisition and expose ourselves to fraud. This should be removed.

