The way to do it will be with the new flag {{--force_online}} to {{proxysql_sync}} via {{userctl}} in usermanager.sqldb

i.e.

{noformat}/opt/v2configless/live/bin/userctl -e prelive -v proxysql_sync --disable --force_online
2024-05-23 11:07:05,082 INFO:[granter.py:797:proxysql_sync] Updating proxysql to force ONLINE
2024-05-23 11:07:05,220 INFO:[granter.py:799:proxysql_sync] S3 object bucket=bolt-proxysql-708712575109-eu-central-1 path='prelive/disable_proxysql_sync.lock' created{noformat}

This option is adding this IN the {{disable_proxysql_sync.lock}} file that we know already.

{noformat}{
    "mysql_servers": {
        "status": "ONLINE"
    },
    "meta": {
        "timestamp": 1716461502.2886379
    }
}{noformat}

Every execution will overwrite this content, therefore we have a different timestamp OR *clean the content leaving an empty file* meaning that we won’t force ONLINE



In the ProxySQL side, When indicated to set all servers ONLINE, *it will do it once only.*
If we need to do it again, we will rerun the command.


The set online is a direct {{UPDATE mysql_servers SET status = 'ONLINE';}} on each ProxySQL node, which is the fastest.

